# DATA repo — campaigns, tenants, libraries, system backlog.
# Operators read and write here; Claude Code drives the git, they never type a command.

# Secrets never enter the repo (team-deployment.md §9.2)
.env
.env.*
credentials.md
**/credentials.md

# Per-machine, never shared (§9.1)
.claude/local/
.claude/state/dirty-campaigns.json
.claude/state/hook-latency.json
.claude/state/license-accepted.json

# Derived surfaces are a CACHE, not information (§10). Under `profile: team` every operator
# renders locally, so committing them only creates a race for the same write target — the
# single largest source of merge conflicts, for files that are a pure function of md + yaml.
*.html

# OS / Python noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# WORKING FILES, never deliverables. Measured on the master 2026-09-02: campaigns/ was
# 6.4 GB, and 90% of it was raw screen captures plus _tmp/ intermediates. The finished
# assets came to 673 MB. Nothing said "do not track these", so they were tracked, and once
# they are in history only a rewrite removes them. These rules are what keeps a new
# deployment at hundreds of megabytes instead of gigabytes.
# Anything a Producer actually SHIPS lives in finals/ or youtube-upload/ and is tracked.
**/_tmp/
**/*Recording*.mp4
**/*Recording*.mov
**/placeholder-screenshots/
**/gallery-thumbs/
node_modules/
.remotion/
dist/
build/
